{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/493141-stupid-crazy-idea-for-the-day","id":493141,"title":"Stupid crazy idea for the day.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-26T19:21:38-07:00","id":493141,"title":"Stupid crazy idea for the day.","content":"750 <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#231F20\">Garou</span></span> (yes, those guys)are dropped worldwide into the Forsaken's universe. No explanation given. Chronicle starts with the Forsaken going about their daily stuff only to start hearing through the spirit grapevine about weird Uratha screaming about &quot;Gaia&quot; and &quot;Worms&quot; and crap. Quickly followed by a series of obvious werewolf attacks on factories and other industrial plants, all within the Protectorate's territory.<br /> <br /> Or perhaps have it be told from the Garou's side. A pack of soldiers going through their operations only to realize that they are no longer actually fighting their enemy. They are in a strange land where the war that they have been dealing with all their lives in no longer applies. The defining aspect of a character cast away because the enemy that you have been fighting is simply gone. Not vanquished but gone. What kind of existential crisis would erupt from this, and who might exploit it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T19:45:35-07:00","id":493168,"title":"","content":"Sounds like dimensional Mage-work to me. A Mage tries to flee into a world where the Wyrm is more in balance, and rips a hole open between the two.<br /> <br /> &quot;...Oops.&quot;<br /> <br /> That, or a rite to raise the Border Marches that's gone horribly, HORRIBLY wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T20:40:06-07:00","id":493191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/493141-stupid-crazy-idea-for-the-day?p=493168#post493168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds like dimensional Mage-work to me. A Mage tries to flee into a world where the Wyrm is more in balance, and rips a hole open between the two.<br /> <br /> &quot;...Oops.&quot;<br /> <br /> That, or a rite to raise the Border Marches that's gone horribly, HORRIBLY wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div> I was planning going to roll with that a Rite preformed within the confines of deactivated God-Machine infrastructure that was previously tinkered with TF:V's Project FORT for inter-dimensional travel is a generally not a good idea. <br /> <br /> Still planning on how the two will interact other than the Forsaken freaking out about the idea that the Predator Kings are wandering around in <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#231F20\">Garou</span></span> form making a mess of their territory while the <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#231F20\">Garou</span></span> are pondering just why the Spirits so wyrm-touched and exhausting themselves beating every single damn spirit into submission.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T20:52:38-07:00","id":493224,"title":"","content":"Werewolf Translation Guide might give you ideas on who would get along with whom. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T21:42:27-07:00","id":493252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/493141-stupid-crazy-idea-for-the-day?p=493224#post493224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolf Translation Guide might give you ideas on who would get along with whom. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>It's what sparked this crazy idea.<br /> <br /> But looking at the concept that is currently playing out, it's less of Translating the <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#231F20\">Garou</span></span> into Uratha and more of simply dropping the Garou into Forsaken's universe as is.<br /> <br /> But all in all, 750 is not enough numbers for a &quot;nation&quot;. Maybe a tribe but all the packs have been dropped world wide and more than a few will die before they realize they aren't fighting their war anymore. Maybe half of those left will &quot;join&quot; the Pure while the others will come sniffing to see what the Forsaken are about.<br /> <br /> I foresee a large subsect of the group continuing to terrorize, rampage, and kill due simply to their inability to see their war as &quot;over&quot;.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T22:30:02-07:00","id":493270,"title":"","content":"Do they keep their Multiple Action Rage abilities?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T02:26:12-07:00","id":493395,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that could be a problem. nWoD just isn't built with them in mind. <br /> <br /> One solution: that aspect of Rage works like oWoD Celerity, sort of, which fortunately enough is a thing in nWoD as well. So we could port the mechanics over from that maybe. <br /> <br /> Would they still take aggravated damage from fire? I mean, back in oWoD it has a noticeable effect on their regeneration, whilst humans basically treated it as lethal. So for consistency it should probably do the same here. Chalk it up to physiology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T19:22:15-07:00","id":494238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/493141-stupid-crazy-idea-for-the-day?p=493395#post493395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, that could be a problem. nWoD just isn't built with them in mind.<br /> <br /> One solution: that aspect of Rage works like oWoD Celerity, sort of, which fortunately enough is a thing in nWoD as well. So we could port the mechanics over from that maybe.<br /> <br /> Would they still take aggravated damage from fire? I mean, back in oWoD it has a noticeable effect on their regeneration, whilst humans basically treated it as lethal. So for consistency it should probably do the same here. Chalk it up to physiology.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll see about getting my hands on Apoc20 later on this week and breaking them down to the point where I can start making Werewolf hacks that give a rough approximation of what the <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#231F20\">Garou</span></span> can do naturally.<br /> <br /> That given, the whole situation would've massively disrupted their ties to spirits (if not outright broke them in places) so Gifts, Totems, and the like would be broken and have to be worked from the ground up again. In short, it's considered an innate power, they got it. Anything that's external is a no go.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T00:23:52-07:00","id":494459,"title":"","content":"They'd presumably have the gifts they came with. Fortunately for them, they're actually capable of teaching <i>each other</i> gifts if they know them. Some of them wouldn't work, because they rely on the presence of Umbral spirits, but others are things like &quot;can jump really high&quot; and those should still work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T09:25:32-07:00","id":494933,"title":"","content":"There was a crossover between werewolf the wyld west and deadlands, which had the premise that there are garou seeking another earth in the umbra to bolster Gaia.<br /> <br /> One can of course do what one wants in their games, but a camp of umbral explorers looking for alternate earths finding one seems a lot easier than dragging the godmachine and hunter into it.<br /> <br /> And it gives the garou a purpose- they want to somehow tie the two earth spirits together, which could have results from draining vitality from nwod (since lets face it, nwod Gaia doesn't seem to have any of the problems of owod Gaia), to creating a spirit highway between the umbra and the shadow, to merging the two worlds like a mystic Amalgam comicbook. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T09:36:11-07:00","id":494941,"title":"","content":"Most of them would join the Pure, right? I could see the Glass Walkers not doing it, but the others seem really amped up in their rage and warmongering. At the least I could see the Pure really idolizing them, with their ability to maintain Crinos and to breed true with wolves or simply be wolves.<br /> <br /> Pangaea certainly seems like a more achievable goal than what they were going for with the Triat, even if it's just a werewolf-ruled post apocalypse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-28-2015, 12:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T10:03:42-07:00","id":494979,"title":"","content":"That really depends on what they think of the whole &quot;reject Luna and auspices&quot; thing. The Garou consider Luna the source of their Rage, the primal spark that makes a werewolf a werewolf. The notion that someone would <i>reject</i> her? Reject the sacred roles she laid down? <br /> <br /> The Garou may well consider the Pure little more than a bunch of rabid dogs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T16:51:09-07:00","id":495394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/493141-stupid-crazy-idea-for-the-day?p=494933#post494933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> There was a crossover between werewolf the wyld west and deadlands, which had the premise that there are garou seeking another earth in the umbra to bolster Gaia.<br /> <br /> One can of course do what one wants in their games, but a camp of umbral explorers looking for alternate earths finding one seems a lot easier than dragging the godmachine and hunter into it.<br /> <br /> And it gives the garou a purpose- they want to somehow tie the two earth spirits together, which could have results from draining vitality from nwod (since lets face it, nwod Gaia doesn't seem to have any of the problems of owod Gaia), to creating a spirit highway between the umbra and the shadow, to merging the two worlds like a mystic Amalgam comicbook.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hum.. Could have the Garou pop out at various points, engage a little with the Uratha, and then fight among themselves if they wish to reconnect this brave new world to theirs (May God help the world because it will not last long at all.) or burn any bridges to prevent anything remotely related to the Wyrm crosses and try to live out their lives without The War consuming their lives.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T23:56:59-07:00","id":496016,"title":"","content":"And perhaps a third faction, who instead of wanting to go with the original plan of merging the Gaias or retiring to a world that for all its problems might very well seem like a paradise to a garou, this third faction might want to do a whole noah's ark thing and bring in as many garou, kinfolk, maybe some friendly bete or dreamspeakers to this brave new world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T18:45:30-07:00","id":496949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/493141-stupid-crazy-idea-for-the-day?p=496016#post496016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And perhaps a third faction, who instead of wanting to go with the original plan of merging the Gaias or retiring to a world that for all its problems might very well seem like a paradise to a garou, this third faction might want to do a whole noah's ark thing and bring in as many garou, kinfolk, maybe some friendly bete or dreamspeakers to this brave new world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps and I could see this happening. However, I can easily see this sparking issues with the Uratha.<br /> <br /> Given that the Uratha are already NIMBY orientated, dealing with the inflow would create issues (Not to mention that the Garou are more combat directed than the Uratha doesn't help) of it if it succeeds at all.<br /> <br /> Another thing to add is that the Garou may end up being changed via length of time in this world. Gaia in nWoD is not the planning entity that it is of oWoD. It's alien, inscrutable and very distant for a being that is the planet. The Uratha have Father Wolf and Luna which their power flows. The Garou may end up being tied to a entity far more alien in thinking than they are used to expecting. Be given a new mission with a purpose so alien to the normal way of Garou thinking that some of them would pause to entertain the thought of going back.<br /> <br /> nWoD is nothing if not full of Dark Mysteries and it only makes sense that if the refugees want to be made permanent residents, they will have to partake in the rent that all the others must pay.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T19:03:03-07:00","id":496959,"title":"","content":"Do werewolves from Apocalypse have silver brands of renown?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T01:22:49-07:00","id":497227,"title":"","content":"Can't find any reference to such in 20th Anniversary Edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T03:34:33-07:00","id":497287,"title":"","content":"If memory serves, garou renown was less formal, more word of mouth getting to the spirits kind of . <br /> <br /> So as to the question of garou getting renown in nwod, one would have to decide how Luna and her lunes handle these foreign werewolves.<br /> <br /> For example, if the lunes, flighty spirits that they are, decide that a werewolf is a werewolf is a werewolf, they might teach the garou the appropriate rites for the stuff they need to know.<br /> <br /> One issue to consider is the future generations of garou. Unless they take their kinfolk with them, they'd probably start looking at wolf-blooded for mating purposes.<br /> <br /> So what effect could that have on garou heredity?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T05:47:40-07:00","id":497358,"title":"","content":"What happens if a Garou breeds with an <i>Uratha? </i>That could potentially get messy. <br /> <br /> I mean maybe any kids will work as if they were native to the nwod, but then there's the Lupus issue. <br /> <br /> Oh, also because Delirium is based on ancestral memories of the Impergium it's going to crap out in a universe where that never happened. Better hope Lunacy picks up the slack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T16:15:40-07:00","id":497964,"title":"","content":"I'd assume it would, (the lunacy) but breeding wouldn't work. The two are clearly different species of werewolves, and I imagine their seeds wouldn't be viable together. Hell the issue of Metis could not be ignored, and even if it could the Garou would be outbred within a few generations. Roughly 10% of their children breed true so by the 3rd generation (Assuming they didnt just prodigiously bone everything around them... and some fianna can do that) the numbers of garou available would probably be less then a handful. <br /> <br /> Knowing that, even if that wasn't a problem their rituals would probably not work in opposing settings worlds, but their gifts would. Not sure about fetishes... I know pound for pound a lone crinos werewolf could physically beat down a long Gauru form uratha, even including healing factor. They're just a far deadlier species (all natural attacks cause aggro damage, unless you're punching something... which could be argued a half ton war beast should cause lethal with a fist), and far more geared for war then the Uratha. They could align themselves together, but I think it's far more likely the garou would go on an ignorant blood hunt. Course they could just live in the world and enjoy the fact that there isn't a wyrm to fight anymore. Uratha in the opposing setting may have a harder time dealing with the great evil of the Wyrm and the weaver, but considering the power of the Idigam they face, it may not be so bad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T16:35:39-07:00","id":497984,"title":"","content":"Uratha in Apocalypse's setting would probably have it a lot easier. They're not as urged on by rage, and they don't have to worry about the idigam or the shartha, they even have potential allies in the other changing breeds and spirits aren't as intent on breaking through to the other side. Take away all those problems and they'd be able to find a clear focus in working against the Wyrm, providing it was necessary, or at least the more baleful of the Wyrm's servants, such as Pentex and the Black Spiral Dancers.<br /> <br /> As it is Uratha have a hard time with Bale Hounds because they could be anywhere, providing you don't use the Dark Pantheism concept. If all the 'bad' werewolves were in one tribe and you didn't have Pure or Bale Hounds to worry about? Man they would be having it easy.<br /> <br /> Of course, they're hunters, not warriors for Gaia. So no guarantee they'd fall in line with the paradigm of the rest of the Garou. And the Garou would probably hunt them down as anathema.<br /> <br /> About the Garou vs Uratha in new World of Darkness' setting, if they did manage to piss off the Pure, which I can't really see happening since they are able to waltz around in 'Father's' form and don't bear the brands of Luna's slavery, the Pure might have the advantage in numbers, since the Pure tend to have larger individual packs. But at that point you get into theoretical logistics, do all the 750 Garou stick together? Are they all in the same area code, or spread across the world in their individual packs, and so forth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-30-2015, 07:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T17:54:37-07:00","id":498047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If memory serves, garou renown was less formal, more word of mouth getting to the spirits kind of .<br /> <br /> So as to the question of garou getting renown in nwod, one would have to decide how Luna and her lunes handle these foreign werewolves.<br /> <br /> For example, if the lunes, flighty spirits that they are, decide that a werewolf is a werewolf is a werewolf, they might teach the garou the appropriate rites for the stuff they need to know.<br /> <br /> One issue to consider is the future generations of garou. Unless they take their kinfolk with them, they'd probably start looking at wolf-blooded for mating purposes.<br /> <br /> So what effect could that have on garou heredity? </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/493141-stupid-crazy-idea-for-the-day?p=497358#post497358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What happens if a Garou breeds with an <i>Uratha? </i>That could potentially get messy.<br /> <br /> I mean maybe any kids will work as if they were native to the nwod, but then there's the Lupus issue.<br /> <br /> Oh, also because Delirium is based on ancestral memories of the Impergium it's going to crap out in a universe where that never happened. Better hope Lunacy picks up the slack.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that 2E Forsaken has really started to do away with the &quot;Wolf Gene&quot; outlook (considering that 1. Wolf Blooded status can be granted if you seemly live to see a high power Uratha and you fail your Lunacy roll, and 2. Luna can simply recruit you into her army because she's a crazy bitch like that), I would consider it a less of an issue.<br /> <br /> Of course, I can see some Garou simply not realizing this and thinking Uratha breeding works as the same as theirs.<br /> <br /> Likewise, I can see Uratha thinking the Garou being... well... They mate with wolves...<br /> <br /> In theory, Delirium being broken should be a bad thing but almost all of humanity has been trained to look to the other way when it comes to this shit so other than perhaps a little bit more activity from Hunter orgs, I don't see much happening.<br /> <br /> However, I've been toying with the Garou stuck here keep their ability such a Delirium but that's mostly because this nWoD Gaia has &quot;plans&quot; for them later which consist of a a trillion voices telling Garou what to do, basically given them schizophrenia via all the different voices.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/493141-stupid-crazy-idea-for-the-day?p=497964#post497964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd assume it would, (the lunacy) but breeding wouldn't work. The two are clearly different species of werewolves, and I imagine their seeds wouldn't be viable together. Hell the issue of Metis could not be ignored, and even if it could the Garou would be outbred within a few generations. Roughly 10% of their children breed true so by the 3rd generation (Assuming they didnt just prodigiously bone everything around them... and some fianna can do that) the numbers of garou available would probably be less then a handful.<br /> <br /> Knowing that, even if that wasn't a problem their rituals would probably not work in opposing settings worlds, but their gifts would. Not sure about fetishes... I know pound for pound a lone crinos werewolf could physically beat down a long Gauru form uratha, even including healing factor. They're just a far deadlier species (all natural attacks cause aggro damage, unless you're punching something... which could be argued a half ton war beast should cause lethal with a fist), and far more geared for war then the Uratha. They could align themselves together, but I think it's far more likely the garou would go on an ignorant blood hunt. Course they could just live in the world and enjoy the fact that there isn't a wyrm to fight anymore. Uratha in the opposing setting may have a harder time dealing with the great evil of the Wyrm and the weaver, but considering the power of the Idigam they face, it may not be so bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could see Garou trying to consolation into an area (after trying to reconnect with each other) for simply community but yeah, Garou, if nothing changes, will be somewhat like the Rhino species is considered today and within a few generations, will be considered &quot;Bigfoot&quot; by the Uratha.<br /> <br /> Which, considering some of the Garou are extremely family fixed, could lead to some very extreme ideas being pushed to increase their numbers.<br /> <br /> As for what the Garou will do. That's up to them. I foresee blood hunts in certain areas of the world and a bit of cooperation in certain areas. Mostly what interested me was what to the Garou have without fighting Weaver/Wyrm. How to bring the Garou out of the macro of oWod and into the micro of nWoD. The image of a soldier fighting in a war or preparing to fight in a war for all his/her life only to be relieved of it by a fluke of Fate. What does that person do with him/her self? From what point does life begin and the war ends? Perhaps it never ends as you pick up a new one.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> About the Garou vs Uratha in new World of Darkness' setting, if they did manage to piss off the Pure, which I can't really see happening since they are able to waltz around in 'Father's' form and don't bear the brands of Luna's slavery, the Pure might have the advantage in numbers, since the Pure tend to have larger individual packs. But at that point you get into theoretical logistics, do all the 750 Garou stick together? Are they all in the same area code, or spread across the world in their individual packs, and so forth. </div> </div> </div>It's not a really a white room fight and yes, they are all over the world but I'm going to assume that after some fumbling around, they'll eventually all group up.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T19:37:34-07:00","id":498120,"title":"","content":"Not having a &quot;multiple actions in a turn&quot; power would mean Forsaken probably wouldn't last too long in CWoD. Those are always must have powers if you have access to them, Garou automatically start with one with the ability to spend Rage points, Uratha, even in Gauru form with it's super healing, wouldn't last too long in a stand up fight. How would the Forsaken react to a Luna that wasn't their spiritual mother?<br /> <br /> Shock, don't forget the Maeljin exist in both worlds, there's another hook for you. The Maeljin are already trying to infect this world and claim it for their own (while claiming slightly different titles or roles in the process), the Garou are here to stop it or die gloriously trying. Fighting the Maeljin and their servants is one of the few things that can get the Forsaken and Pure to work together. Now you have a reason for everyone to interact in some way. I'm sure the Garou will think the infighting between Forsaken and Pure is a sure sign they are mad from Luna's parentage rather than Gaia's.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T20:51:26-07:00","id":498246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/493141-stupid-crazy-idea-for-the-day?p=498120#post498120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not having a &quot;multiple actions in a turn&quot; power would mean Forsaken probably wouldn't last too long in CWoD. Those are always must have powers if you have access to them, Garou automatically start with one with the ability to spend Rage points, Uratha, even in Gauru form with it's super healing, wouldn't last too long in a stand up fight. How would the Forsaken react to a Luna that wasn't their spiritual mother?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Forsaken in oWoD would be less mechanically able to fight via the way that Gauru do but be much more focused on underpinning weak points and harrying the prey. The entire mindset of the Uratha is to stalk a target, find it's pain points, and amplify them until the time the killing blow is served.<br /> <br /> With this mindset, who knows. They could perhaps leverage the same market forces that prop up Pentex against it within a few months and wield it just as effectively on a local level. Perhaps.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/493141-stupid-crazy-idea-for-the-day?p=498120#post498120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shock, don't forget the Maeljin exist in both worlds, there's another hook for you. The Maeljin are already trying to infect this world and claim it for their own (while claiming slightly different titles or roles in the process), the Garou are here to stop it or die gloriously trying. Fighting the Maeljin and their servants is one of the few things that can get the Forsaken and Pure to work together. Now you have a reason for everyone to interact in some way. I'm sure the Garou will think the infighting between Forsaken and Pure is a sure sign they are mad from Luna's parentage rather than Gaia's.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm holding back commenting on the Maeljin mostly due to lack of knowledge on how oWoD treats them and how Forsaken views the Maeljin not was a world spanning world domination via the Adversary (though that does come up in Inferno) but rather:<br /> <br /> &quot;You know that basket ball court behind 3rd and Marson? Gangs have been using it as a killing field. Fucking executions happening every Friday. Shit's fucked up but when you look at the Shadow, shits even more fucked up and bullshit. We were slowly whittling away at it but had to deal with that rat infestation... Just stay two blocks away and you should be good. Anything less and you're beating on the gates of Hell.&quot;<br /> <br /> And by and large, there isn't so much as impending doom as there is in oWoD. You care less than the world is ending and care more about that fact that you're shaking to hold back the Rage due to some cranky landlord handing you the notice to move out because your dumbass packmate forgot to pay the rent on time when you were out scoping that Azlu's nest. All the while clearly remember the last time this happened. Oh and that gaping maw of Hell that is oh so incrementally growing a few blocks away is the 32rd thing on your mind today while kicking your packmate's ass has firmly taken the express lane to the top.<br /> <br /> It can be handled a bit more differently for the Garou but I like to capture that local feel.<br /> <br /> As for the Maeljin, I like the overall concept that the nWod Maeljin are much more autonomous in actions to the points where they spend most of their time infighting(to the point where it makes the Seers/Kindred look sane) than waging an overarching war (which the arrogantly think they've already won) but then again, fighting with each other simply spreads more sin in the process which serves their overall goal.<br /> <br /> So, in short, the Maeljin are an obvious enemy are worth having the limited number of Garou while the remaining issue is Gaia. From my limited research, I seems like Apoc went with the Green Mother route. I could throw a few Garou in nWoD into a whirl if the Gaia of it requests to have them aid in the Anthropocene.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":604,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","user":"Shock","date":". 05-01-2015, 12:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T01:27:44-07:00","id":498492,"title":"","content":"I'm well aware that Luna decides who becomes a werewolf in nwod, but, and it doesn't matter how one becomes wolf-blooded including lunacy, being wolf-blooded is an inherited trait.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T03:49:53-07:00","id":498601,"title":"","content":"Do garou have any means of pushing past the 5 dot limit for base stats? I couldn't find any reference to it in the book but I may have missed something. <br /> <br /> If not, do you think that will tip the balance at all? There comes a point where it doesn't really matter how many times you swing at a dude, you're just not going to hit him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T07:48:10-07:00","id":498830,"title":"","content":"Totems can do it. Fenris adds dots for attributes that will push you over.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T08:42:40-07:00","id":498922,"title":"","content":"Ok, but forsaken totems can do that too so that cancels out. Nothing else? No power stat equivalent like generation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T13:01:27-07:00","id":499279,"title":"","content":"Not that I temenber. Rank does something with rage but that requires longetivity that most garou don't have. They usually die before 30","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T16:53:51-07:00","id":499497,"title":"","content":"If Farou get multiple actions from rage, then. I think that they also shouldn't have a defense stat, and have to dedicate dodge actions to avoid being hit. Equalizes things pretty well, right there. Combine that with only ever having seven health levels, and no way for an 8 die pool soak can handle the 8 minimum damage hit that any five purity werewolf can put down, and I think that Garou are in trouble.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3347-wild-eyes","name":"Wild-Eyes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T17:02:15-07:00","id":499505,"title":"","content":"That's a point. Garou may get multiple actions per turn, but by the rules they need to use one to attack, one to defend, and in W20 at least one to move more than a few feet. That's two rage points every turn for something Uratha (and everyone else in the nwod) get to do for free. <br /> <br /> Which is why I suggested swapping out the multiple actions for some equivalent power last page. Because used as-is it makes a lot of assumptions about the system that don't hold.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T17:50:34-07:00","id":499554,"title":"","content":"Been thinking about on how Gaia works in nWoD. (with it's tradition of inverting oWoD concepts on it's head) brings me to the following.<br /> <br /> 1) Gaia is Old.<br /> 2) Gaia is Uncaring.<br /> 3) Gaia is Rageful<br /> 4) Gaia, at times, is Cruel.<br /> <br /> Gaia is old is the statement is that the planet' history is so expansive that we are simply a blink in the eye. The dinos were just 4 mins away. A mote in God's eye.<br /> <br /> Gaia is uncaring simply is the statement that nature, as a whole, doesn't give a shit. Gaia has suffered 5 Mass Extinction events (including one where 90% of Life died) as long as life has been around. The idea that humanity's activity's in causing species to die off would get her to care is absurd. Survival of the fittest and all must be tested.<br /> <br /> Gaia is rageful means that the sometimes, the planet feels the need to wipe something off the map. It's the psycho hobo who smiles at you while waving a bloody knife out in the Wal-Mart parking lot at 3 am. No real meaning or rhyme. Just a plain &quot;Fuck this place.&quot;<br /> <br /> Gaia, lastly, is sometimes cruel. Doesn't need to be said how cruel nature can be at times. <br /> <br /> So in the end, I have a spirit who is basically an insane old testament god who doesn't follow her own rules and like her sister Luna, is very likely to cut you if you say the wrong thing.<br /> <br /> That being said, Gaia has a lot to offer the Garou and can certain solidify their hold in keeping a active presence in nWoD. They just have to prove it first.<br /> <br /> Which may end up breaking them as Gaia keeps ordering them to fight against things simply to prove their worth to exist.<br /> <br /> So what's the thought on this?<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T18:57:12-07:00","id":499642,"title":"","content":"I don't know if it's ever been shown that Gaia actually does anything. In this case she might be more like the new testament god, content to let humans have free will even if it means they plunder her and kill each other off. There's one theory that the Breath from Predators is an aspect of Gaia but nothing else as far as I can remember. So I question where the rageful comes in, and I think cruelty is encompassed by uncaring.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T19:35:33-07:00","id":499666,"title":"","content":"You lot ain't conprehending garou power in play. Let's go with attack examples. To strike is usually diff 6 or so, so you use dex+brawl for claw attack (say an average of 3 dex + 3 brawl) you've got 6 dice to strike. You need 1 success to hit, and any extras ADD to the damage roll. <br /> <br /> Damage is then whatever stated per attack so let's use Crinos claw ( pretty sure it's str+2 aggravated) so you've got as an average 3 strength. So 5 dice, plus possibly an additional 5 dice, plus re rolling 10's. With a conservative 3 str you could be doing 10+ damage dice. and at char creation you can easily get 5 dots of strength so... Cwod is a lot more liberal with the initial points. <br /> <br /> As for defense roll you apply stamina as soak so you roll stamina to negate any successes on the opposing side, and apply damage as usual. Garou heal 1 bashing/lethal per turn, not just bashing. <br /> <br /> Multiple actions work on rage points (scale of 1-10) and you can only use half as many rounded up as you have permanent rage stat (there's permanent rage and temporary). Temporary could get you to 10, but you could only use 2 per turn if you had 3 rage as your perm. With 2 rage though it is an additional 2 turns which is a good deal of damage dealt, with no dice handicap for multiple actions (I.rle. Dice splitting). My wife's black spiral is deadly efficient in combat, especially merged with the unicorn spirit like she is. Any uratha is going to have an insanely hard time dealing with that level of power, kuruth or not.<br /> <br /> They also have frenzy, which works like kuruth, but gives you the opportunity to heal any/all damage based on your rage roll. <br /> <br /> I'm all for uratha beating garou in a lot of ways, but pack on pack it just ain't gonna happen. Uratha are hunters and garou are essentially the planets jihadists against damn near anything. In their timeline they almost exterminated all other changing breeds in a rather brutal genocide. If doing a cross over I highly suggest sticking with the gameplay system you know and not trying to mix the two. <br /> <br /> Red sticks would still destroy em all though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T20:32:06-07:00","id":499712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/493141-stupid-crazy-idea-for-the-day?p=499642#post499642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know if it's ever been shown that Gaia actually does anything. In this case she might be more like the new testament god, content to let humans have free will even if it means they plunder her and kill each other off. There's one theory that the Breath from Predators is an aspect of Gaia but nothing else as far as I can remember. So I question where the rageful comes in, and I think cruelty is encompassed by uncaring.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. Mostly was using Rage with the icon of natural disasters at times but meh.<br /> <br /> I am mostly just brainstorming ways to make nWoD Gaia more active in terms of making a pact that the Garou may find distasteful.<br /> <br /> What reason would have a spirit who is mostly apathetic to the way the world is, be spurred into action and offer to a patron to a new breed of wolfish shapeshifters?<br /> <br /> Granted said duties of said pack are less defend the world from spiritual oblivion and more playing eternal wack-a-mole with the other forces with no real hope of a end point.<br /> <br /> edit:<br /> Looking back at it. I see Gaia being either &quot;dead&quot; or inattentive. It may be a long term plan for the Remnant of the Garou but many short term ones remain. Creating a Sept, understanding how Loci work, processing how Spirits now act, and forging deals with the spirit world (granted how spirits act in nWoD, it would be very one sided in the spirit's favor).<br /> <br /> And after looking at it some more, I've started to think the reason why the Garou are in nWoD is that oWoD simply broke at the time of the Wyrm's victory, throwing things into &quot;what is&quot; and &quot;what shouldn't be but is.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Garou just managed to keep somewhat sane in the Abyss only to be vomited up on the shores of the reality of nWoD. A People with no historical relevance, and no Fate. Their war has morphed from one of world spanning conflict to one of simply everyday survival in a world that is stacked against them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":604,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","user":"Shock","date":". 05-02-2015, 01:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T05:04:19-07:00","id":506620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/493141-stupid-crazy-idea-for-the-day?p=499712#post499712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True. Mostly was using Rage with the icon of natural disasters at times but meh.<br /> <br /> I am mostly just brainstorming ways to make nWoD Gaia more active in terms of making a pact that the Garou may find distasteful.<br /> <br /> What reason would have a spirit who is mostly apathetic to the way the world is, be spurred into action and offer to a patron to a new breed of wolfish shapeshifters?<br /> <br /> Granted said duties of said pack are less defend the world from spiritual oblivion and more playing eternal wack-a-mole with the other forces with no real hope of a end point.<br /> <br /> edit:<br /> Looking back at it. I see Gaia being either &quot;dead&quot; or inattentive. It may be a long term plan for the Remnant of the Garou but many short term ones remain. Creating a Sept, understanding how Loci work, processing how Spirits now act, and forging deals with the spirit world (granted how spirits act in nWoD, it would be very one sided in the spirit's favor).<br /> <br /> And after looking at it some more, I've started to think the reason why the Garou are in nWoD is that oWoD simply broke at the time of the Wyrm's victory, throwing things into &quot;what is&quot; and &quot;what shouldn't be but is.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Garou just managed to keep somewhat sane in the Abyss only to be vomited up on the shores of the reality of nWoD. A People with no historical relevance, and no Fate. Their war has morphed from one of world spanning conflict to one of simply everyday survival in a world that is stacked against them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Why not just go with indifference? Gaia doesn't care, that's all. No matter how many corrupted spirits you kill or how many factories you destroy she doesn't give a fuck. You your packmates and all that 'war' thingy are all microbes on the body of a god. even worse if she get's annoyed for bothering her, how traumatising when Gaia punishes devoted werewolf (or demands human sacrifices). Cold indifference may be more hurting. Some would try fanatically to try her approval, some would tun to other gods and some may just become lost and dispassionate. <br /> <br /> Of course there is the question of all the nature spirits which have become inhuman, uncaring for life, very greedy and way more bloodthirsty (there was a mention of river spirits demanding yearly human sacrifices). Than there is a little fact that nWod spirits don't die when at 0 corpus, a nasty surprise for Garou. Also, all the emotional and abstract spirits confined to Astral realm in oWoD are now in an equivalent of Penumbra.<br /> <br /> Also, they don't exist alone. What if they try to wrestle hallows from mages? (for defiling gaia or some other BS). Or maybe they go in a vampire killing spree or harass local fera. How will they see local Geist and Prometheans? Something tell's me they'll think them as new fomor. Plus there are entities not known in oWod cosmology. Some of the Exarchs may want new pets, Abyss may dupe new guys that know nothing of it (way weirder than Wyrm), some may try to contact Thyrsus thinking they are Dreamspeakers, or put contracts with Gentry (Wild spirits), and just imagine some of them finding Avernian Gates.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T13:17:44-07:00","id":507109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/493141-stupid-crazy-idea-for-the-day?p=506620#post506620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why not just go with indifference? Gaia doesn't care, that's all. No matter how many corrupted spirits you kill or how many factories you destroy she doesn't give a fuck. You your packmates and all that 'war' thingy are all microbes on the body of a god. even worse if she get's annoyed for bothering her, how traumatising when Gaia punishes devoted werewolf (or demands human sacrifices). Cold indifference may be more hurting. Some would try fanatically to try her approval, some would tun to other gods and some may just become lost and dispassionate.<br /> <br /> Of course there is the question of all the nature spirits which have become inhuman, uncaring for life, very greedy and way more bloodthirsty (there was a mention of river spirits demanding yearly human sacrifices). Than there is a little fact that nWod spirits don't die when at 0 corpus, a nasty surprise for Garou. Also, all the emotional and abstract spirits confined to Astral realm in oWoD are now in an equivalent of Penumbra.<br /> <br /> Also, they don't exist alone. What if they try to wrestle hallows from mages? (for defiling gaia or some other BS). Or maybe they go in a vampire killing spree or harass local fera. How will they see local Geist and Prometheans? Something tell's me they'll think them as new fomor. Plus there are entities not known in oWod cosmology. Some of the Exarchs may want new pets, Abyss may dupe new guys that know nothing of it (way weirder than Wyrm), some may try to contact Thyrsus thinking they are Dreamspeakers, or put contracts with Gentry (Wild spirits), and just imagine some of them finding Avernian Gates.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am going with indifference now. I've been constructing the idea of how the Garou would act. As it currently stands. I have them being dropped all over the world and then converging on the place that was oWoD's final battleground.<br /> <br /> Running theory was that the Wyrm/Oblivion won in the final battle and in the height of it's victory, the universe terminated. Everything broke down. The Garou had themselves swimming in the Abyss (oWoD's Abyss and nWod's Abyss are the same for the sake of the game) until being vomited up onto the grounds of nWoD.<br /> <br /> As such, with their limited numbers, they are simply making the first and last sept of the Garou nation on the area of the final battleground (going to be left unstated for the STs to place around but assume the area between New Mexico and Denver).<br /> <br /> The Tribes are without totems but are still kinda considered tribes. In the same manner that a group of people are considered a club even if they don't have a clubhouse. I have have yet to work that out the mechanics but the politics comes as follows:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Children of Gaia would turn into a quasi religious organization focused on getting in contact with Gaia or waking her from slumber.<br /> <br /> The Black Furies would be very influential on the leadership of the Sept mostly due to them being able to use breeding and protection of the young as leverage.<br /> <br /> The Bone Gnawers would spend their time mostly outside the sept other than using it as a occasional safe haven and dropping off information about threats to it.<br /> <br /> The Fianna would be busy being obsessed with documenting all of the Garou's oral history while the members who still carry it still exist.<br /> <br /> The Get of Fenris would be nursing their wounds after getting their asses kicked via their first swing at spirits and more focused on material enemies such as Uratha and humans that threaten the nation.<br /> <br /> The Glass Walkers would expand into massive projects that may or may not get them kicked out the Garou nation. One of which is to take a page out of Magadon's playbook and use vaccines to create Kinfolk who will later turn into Garou.<br /> <br /> The Red Talons would be welcome at first but have their welcome start to wear thin after a while (mostly by bringing Law Enforcement attention onto the Nation in it's very weak state.) May or may not run off with the Predator Kings.<br /> <br /> The Shadow Lords would emerge as the top &quot;tribe&quot; given the Sliver Fangs emerged in a weakened state than they and have made the convincing argument that if the Garou nation is going to survive, extensive changes to favor brains over brawn must be made.<br /> <br /> The Silent Striders would become start to be quite adapt at exploring the Shadow and most likely (along with the Gets, although they learned from a more painful manner) learn how spirits work and how the Shadow operates as a whole, quickly becoming an analog for the Uratha Bone Shadows.<br /> <br /> The Sliver Fangs are struggling to keep relevant while most of their members suffer from Harano not from Gaia's suffering but rather from the fact that they have completely lost their history, lineage, and kinfolk supporting them. May or may not make a comeback.<br /> <br /> The Stargazers.. I don't really how they would adapt other than perhaps working with the Children of Gaia mostly to find another &quot;caern&quot; (Massive locus with positive essence). Other tribes would view them with distrust as they stories of them pulling out when the Nation needed them most persist.<br /> <br /> The Uktena and the Wendigo would merge due to the lack of enough members in both tribes and carve out a spot in the nation as effective assassins of the Nation while still trying to forge a connection to the native people around the area. </div> </div> </div>In this, I would farther condense these groups down into themes:<br /> <br /> Explorers/Shadow Meddlers: Children of Gaia, The Bone Gnawers, The Silent Striders, and The Stargazers. Most likely for the Uratha to see bumbling around the Shadow and causing trouble.<br /> <br /> Politics/Sept home: Fianna, Get of Fenris, Shadow Lords, Black Furies, and Sliver Fangs. Basically focusing on the politics of the Sept.<br /> <br /> Big issues: Glass Walkers, Red Talons. Issues of those tribes that may or may not get them exiled.<br /> <br /> Wildcards: Uktena and the Wendigo.<br /> <br /> Edit: as much as the translation guide does help, it's still rather hard to take groups which are mostly based on location/certain culture and transfer them into purpose-driven groups.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":604,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","user":"Shock","date":". 05-07-2015, 04:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T13:26:40-07:00","id":507113,"title":"","content":"I could see the Glass Walkers investigating heavily into the God Machine, which is vaguely similar to the Weaver.<br /> <br /> The Red Talons seem like they'd go to war with humanity or join the Pure, seeing their possible inability to mate with wolves as some sort of curse.<br /> <br /> Would the others still hate vampires?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-07-2015, 04:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T13:39:19-07:00","id":507118,"title":"","content":"On the one hand, no wyrm taint. <br /> <br /> On the other, still bloodsucking walking corpses. <br /> <br /> Could go either way really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T13:57:08-07:00","id":507169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/493141-stupid-crazy-idea-for-the-day?p=507113#post507113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could see the Glass Walkers investigating heavily into the God Machine, which is vaguely similar to the Weaver.<br /> <br /> The Red Talons seem like they'd go to war with humanity or join the Pure, seeing their possible inability to mate with wolves as some sort of curse.<br /> <br /> Would they still hate vampires?</div> </div> </div> </div>Glass Walkers as a whole, don't know much about the God-Machine or really anything in nWoD. Most of the tribes, at best, are only 60 to 75 members. It's implied that the God-Machine could take a interest in what amounts to be a huge spike on it's readings and sending an angel to go find out what happened and then work on from there but yeah. Most of the Glass Walkers will simply assume this is the Weaver talking to them and will react accordingly.<br /> <br /> The Garou in general still believe the Triat is still operating. This will change as the years progress and what they believe ends up in the same boat as a Garou based religion complete with disbelievers.<br /> <br /> As for the Red Talons, as the Garou are being dropped in nWoD as is, it's implied that they can mate with wolves just fine and yes, a few of them will cross over to joining the Pure full time while others will stay with the Sept. It's less of outright exile as it is a family member storming out of the house in a heated argument. They are still welcome in the sept, the trouble that they bring isn't though.<br /> <br /> The Vampire question is most likely yes due to belief in the Wyrm. However, the problem is that the Garou who have the ability to use &quot;sense Wyrd, Sense Wyrm, and Sense Weaver.&quot; on spirits (any spirit in general) get the same response. &quot;yes, yes, and yes&quot;. Which means to them that the spirit is all part of the Triat operating and this happens for every spirit they do it on. So over time, more than a few Garou will start to doubt if the Wyrm is working through the Kindred or even if the Wyrm as a active spirit is around at all.<br /> <br /> Given Uratha relations with the Kindred (Uratha as a whole, cull the Neonates, bargain with the Ancilla, and stay the hell from Elders<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Bold\">)</span></span>, the Garou going around wrecking the place would cause a few feathers to be ruffled in the Danse Macabre and cause a few headaches for Uratha protectorates who have contacts with the Kindred.<br /> <br /> As for mechanics, I'm figuring keeping the duel Rage and Gnosis as spendable points that can be regained through acquiring beats (Rage) and achieving long term spiritual aspirations (Gnosis). Still toying with the idea though.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":604,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","user":"Shock","date":". 05-07-2015, 06:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T14:02:19-07:00","id":507173,"title":"","content":"Why would spirits test positive for the triat though?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T14:08:04-07:00","id":507180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/493141-stupid-crazy-idea-for-the-day?p=507173#post507173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would spirits test positive for the triat though?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mostly because they are beings of raw creation, are weaved in shapes and compose themselves into instinctive hierarchies, and feast on each other in a orgy of violence.<br /> <br /> And plus, I just like planting dark mysteries so <i>why are the spirits testing positive for the Triat? </i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T14:35:54-07:00","id":507226,"title":"","content":"Ok, that's a good point. <br /> <br /> But just for giggles lets have the Idigam as not register as any.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T14:47:09-07:00","id":507236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/493141-stupid-crazy-idea-for-the-day?p=507226#post507226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, that's a good point.<br /> <br /> But just for giggles lets have the Idigam as not register as any.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now that is something that would really through the Garou into a loop.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T15:17:10-07:00","id":507265,"title":"","content":"Considering their constant changing nature, wouldn't they resonate with the wyrd? Wyld? Between Apocalypse, Exalted and Changeling I can never keep track of which is which.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T15:21:02-07:00","id":507269,"title":"","content":"Wyld. Yeah, they probably would, but I just figured their nature makes the magic garou senses just sort of give up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T15:22:54-07:00","id":507271,"title":"","content":"I like that too. But the idea of them thinking the idigam are some last vestige of their wyld and something to serve would be amusing but probably not the way Shock wants to go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T15:40:10-07:00","id":507289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/493141-stupid-crazy-idea-for-the-day?p=507265#post507265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering their constant changing nature, wouldn't they resonate with the wyrd? Wyld? Between Apocalypse, Exalted and Changeling I can never keep track of which is which.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wyld, in terms of Apocalypse, is associated with creation and the like. Wyrd is associated with Fate in Changeling the Lost.<br /> <br /> But yes. Normally they would but not having them trigger as on any &quot;wyrm, weaver, and wyld&quot; implies that something is more alien about them than the normal &quot;Creation, Stasis, Destruction.&quot; that all the spirits seem to have. The Uratha may have clues but until the Garou and the Uratha start comparing notes, they aren't really going to know why that is happening.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T15:43:09-07:00","id":507293,"title":"","content":"One thing's for sure. They're not of the Weaver.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T16:04:22-07:00","id":507331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/493141-stupid-crazy-idea-for-the-day?p=507271#post507271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like that too. But the idea of them thinking the idigam are some last vestige of their wyld and something to serve would be amusing but probably not the way Shock wants to go.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ironically, I was toying with this idea as well very much and it would be very amusing that the Garou were serving the wyld in oWoD when the Uratha are having to go up against it but doing it the other way highlights the alien-like nature of the Idigam which is excellent for making the Garou go &quot;WTF is that?! We hurt it, we kill it, we do everything and the motherfucker keeps coming back!&quot;<br /> <br /> I'll have to flip a coin on the matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":604,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","user":"Shock","date":". 05-07-2015, 07:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T17:53:50-07:00","id":507426,"title":"","content":"I would use the Triat as Idigam. Specifically with their soul corrupting capabilities (Black spiral dancers to the Wyrm as those hollowed out wolves are to the Idigam).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T21:31:29-07:00","id":507629,"title":"","content":"Well that doesn't quite work, since not all black spiral dancers are possessed.<br /> <br /> One thing to keep in mind is that nwod must have native versions of the triat- There must be a spirit of entropy, a spirit of order, and a spirit of chaos.<br /> <br /> However, if they are at war, no one has noticed. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> So the garou could seek out the spirit of chaos, and if there are any glasswalkers in the group, perhaps order too, to make alliances. A paranoid garou might look up the spirit of entropy just to make sure there isn't a wyrm 2.0 lying in wait.<br /> <br /> Since these guys aren't covered, the garou could be as surprised as one likes in this scenario.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T23:00:43-07:00","id":507726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/493141-stupid-crazy-idea-for-the-day?p=507629#post507629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Well that doesn't quite work, since not all black spiral dancers are possessed.<br /> <br /> One thing to keep in mind is that nwod must have native versions of the triat- There must be a spirit of entropy, a spirit of order, and a spirit of chaos.<br /> <br /> However, if they are at war, no one has noticed. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> So the garou could seek out the spirit of chaos, and if there are any glasswalkers in the group, perhaps order too, to make alliances. A paranoid garou might look up the spirit of entropy just to make sure there isn't a wyrm 2.0 lying in wait.<br /> <br /> Since these guys aren't covered, the garou could be as surprised as one likes in this scenario.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> doesn't Abyss already cover Wyrm? (and than some more)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T23:44:35-07:00","id":507749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/493141-stupid-crazy-idea-for-the-day?p=507629#post507629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Well that doesn't quite work, since not all black spiral dancers are possessed.<br /> <br /> One thing to keep in mind is that nwod must have native versions of the triat- There must be a spirit of entropy, a spirit of order, and a spirit of chaos.<br /> <br /> However, if they are at war, no one has noticed. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>The Triat does exist to an extent but really only in abstract form. The Weaver never awoken and went insane trying to ensnare the Wyrm and likewise threw it insane and the like. The Shadow, when you look at it, incorporates all their elements equally and thus a more accurate way of putting it is if someone broke down the oWoD Triat, and create a system of which all of three members are expressed but yet are so divided against each other that they can't work as a whole like they did before.<br /> <br /> edit: so basically the Triat is a group of slumbering God-Spirits who have yet to reach critical mass of essence to be &quot;born&quot; or &quot;awakened&quot; even if they exist in the Shadow as concepts and the Shadow's dark animalism seems to prevent exactly that from happening.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/493141-stupid-crazy-idea-for-the-day?p=507726#post507726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">doesn't Abyss already cover Wyrm? (and than some more)</div> </div> </div> </div>Wyrm, from my understanding, works like like a Aeon of the Death Arcanum when it's working normally and a creature of the Lower Depths when it isn't. It reaching into the Abyss in the last world was simply a mad desire to undo the universe to such an extent that the Abyss was leaking through wholesale.<br /> <br /> But overall, it's a being with a purpose for existing so it's not an Abyssal creature/spirit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":604,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","user":"Shock","date":". 05-08-2015, 02:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T00:19:04-07:00","id":507771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/493141-stupid-crazy-idea-for-the-day?p=507749#post507749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wyrm, from my understanding, works like like a Aeon of the Death Arcanum when it's working normally and a creature of the Lower Depths when it isn't. It reaching into the Abyss in the last world was simply a mad desire to undo the universe to such an extent that the Abyss was leaking through wholesale.<br /> <br /> But overall, it's a being with a purpose for existing so it's not an Abyssal creature/spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean functionally, not philosophically. If you need a cosmic enemy for the garou here it is. It works to defile and destroy the planet and is at least as 'evil' as wyrm. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T02:29:48-07:00","id":507889,"title":"","content":"Wounds and the Mael-Jin would likely also fit that bill, especially with their focus on corruption/transgression.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3347-wild-eyes","name":"Wild-Eyes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T08:41:02-07:00","id":508122,"title":"","content":"Yes, the Inferno seems like it would fit better, but the Inferno doesn't want to destroy, possibly, it wants to corrupt. The Abyss doesn't necessarily want to destroy, that's just a side effect of its true goal, it wants to exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T14:46:29-07:00","id":508434,"title":"","content":"So I got a Chronicle running through my head about the Glass Walkers that goes like this.<br /> <br /> Glass Walkers gets contacted by the God-Machine to solve their population issue via an Angel. Agree but keep it hush-hush.<br /> <br /> ----- Deva Corporation fonts the project. Cue a couple of months. Unchained attack and the like while the GM tells the Glass Walkers it needs a Garou to reduce to bare atoms to scan, document, and replicate the Garou condition (it plans on using vaccines as genetic engineering). After much arguing, they capture a Red Talon to use for the sacrifice<br /> <br /> .-----Everything goes well and good until one of the cultists heading the project drops the bomb that while the first run is only going to effect 10,000 people, the next will be given out nation wide. Glass walker does the math in his head and ends up with the thing potentially causing 31 million people to turn into Garou. Bricks are shat with the Glass Walker stating there is no way that the nation can handle them all, let alone educate them. Cultist agrees and states that the GM intends to send angels to build up tribes that follow it's ideals instead of the Nation's. Cue the Glass Walker attempting to damage the project with an Angel telling him the first run is already in production before kicking him out on his ass.<br /> <br /> -------Glass Walker goes back to tell the others, they get frustrated over getting fucked over and get a call. A ring of Unchained want to meet them<br /> <br /> ----The Unchained meet them and ponder ways to derail the project. Mentions of government contracts with vaccines come up but side with a demon (lawyer) calling up a client at one of Deva's rivals for help.<br /> <br /> -------LDI exec comes in and negotiates with them (with the Unchained mediating) for a &quot;suicide gene&quot; to inflict on the second batch of Deva's vaccine, resulting in the recipient dying instead of being turned into Kinfolk. LDI requests that a certain creature be captured and delivered to them in exchange. Glass Walkers bring up civilian casualties, exec states that is of no consequence and give them a picture and a location.<br /> <br /> -----Cue Glass Walkers getting their asses kicked by an Arisen and vice versa.<br /> <br /> ----Dead Arisen gets delivered and LDI hands over the vial.<br /> <br /> ------Glass Walkers go back to learn the first part of the plan has already been completed (10,000 people are now Kinfolk. One out of ten become Garou) with the second part in production. They, with great effort, get the plans to make the untainted vaccine and corrupt the GM's Command and Control to produce the tainted version.<br /> <br /> ------Cue a couple of months and Deva's in the news about how it lost government contracts to make vaccines to LDI and The Cheiron Group when it's vaccine up and killed a few thousand people. Glass Walkers come back to the Nation with the plans on how to make Kinfolk in hand and keep it a secret among the tribe. Cue the leader of the tribe getting as drunk as a werewolf can while screaming about how bitter the taste of victory is and having to be escorted off the street before the cops pick him up.<br /> <br /> ---Chronicle ends with the Nation freaking out about a thousand new Garou having their first change left and right without any blood relations with Glass Walkers having sad pained frowny faces all the while. Elsewhere, Two Angels discuss the outcome of the project and agree to put the project on hold until they can rediscover the plans that the Glass Walkers have in their possession. They move on to other projects. There are always more projects.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}